{"name":"Wagon Wheel","hex":"#c2b79e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wagon wheel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The wheel of a wagon, including railway wagons.","The wooden spoked wheel of a horse-drawn wagon as often used in centuries past."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wagon_wheel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wagon","blocks":[{"text":"A wagon is a heavy four-wheeled vehicle pulled by draft animals or on occasion by humans, used for transporting goods, commodities, agricultural materials, supplies and sometimes people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Wagon_Ride_P9190071.jpg/330px-Wagon_Ride_P9190071.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagon"},{"title":"Wagon Wheels","blocks":[{"text":"Wagon Wheels are a sweet snack food sold in the United Kingdom as well as other Commonwealth countries such as Australia, Canada, New Zealand, Malta and India. They are also sold in Ireland. They consist of two biscuits that form a sandwich with a marshmallow filling, and they are covered with a chocolate-flavoured coating."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Wagon_Wheel.JPG/330px-Wagon_Wheel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagon_Wheels"},{"title":"Wagon Wheel (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Wagon Wheel\" is a song co-written by Bob Dylan and Ketch Secor of Old Crow Medicine Show. Dylan recorded the chorus in 1973 while Secor added verses 25 years later. Old Crow Medicine Show's final version was certified triple Platinum by the Recording Industry Association of America in 2023. The song has been covered numerous times, including charting versions by Nathan Carter in 2012, Darius Rucker in 2013 and Nathan Evans in 2022."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/OCMS_-_Wagon_Wheel_cd_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagon_Wheel_(song)"},{"title":"Wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A wheel is a rotating component intended to turn on an axle bearing. The wheel is one of the key components of the wheel and axle, which is one of the six simple machines. Wheels, in conjunction with axles, allow heavy objects to be moved easily, facilitating transportation, supporting loads, and performing work in machines. Wheels are also used for other purposes, such as a ship's wheel, steering wheel, potter's wheel, and flywheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg/330px-Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Yerevan%2C_National_History_Museum_of_Armenia_%282%29.jpg/500px-Yerevan%2C_National_History_Museum_of_Armenia_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Yerevan%2C_National_History_Museum_of_Armenia_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Yerevan%2C_National_History_Museum_of_Armenia_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Yerevan%2C_National_History_Museum_of_Armenia_%282%29.jpg/500px-Yerevan%2C_National_History_Museum_of_Armenia_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the two wagons in the History Museum of Armenia, the world's oldest known wagons.[5]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYerevan%2C_National_History_Museum_of_Armenia_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Walraversijde27.jpg/500px-Walraversijde27.jpg?utm_sourc